<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">British India</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> refers to the territories of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-subcontinent">Indian subcontinent</a> ruled directly by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, first through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> and from 1858 by the crown. It expanded by conquest and annexation, absorbing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a> after the Anglo-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> wars of the 1840s. Its northwestern frontier was the focus of rivalry with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>, known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-great-game">Great Game</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/british-india.jpg" alt="British India" width="320" height="263" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Elisha Kirkall (c. 1682–1742) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fort_William,_Calcutta,_1735.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
